They were competing against another team in an online game with their friends, most of whom were childhood friends they had grown up with and gone to school with. They had been playing the game together for almost two years and had formed their own team. The match started smoothly, and everyone was excited. It became a close 2-2 fight with one point left to decide the winner. Everyone looked to them as the best player among their friends, so they began directing the team on what to do and what to expect from their enemies. It was a five-on-five team game, and although their team started to fail and grew demoralized, they tried and did their best. Maneuvering through each of the enemy's attacks with skill and some luck, they dodged and countered them, and before they knew it, they won.